Provider setup wizard in the view

The extension started the provider setup on its own on first load, as a
series of VS Code QuickPicks and InputBoxes. Now nothing starts until the
user presses Get Started on the welcome page (or runs /auth or the auth
command), and the setup runs as a wizard inside the extension's view with
the same steps: provider, protocol, OpenAI API, base URL or endpoint, API
key, models, advanced config. Choice steps advance on a click; input steps on
Next or Enter, with Back and Cancel (Escape) throughout.

The host still owns the provider registry and validation: `auth` sends the
offered providers' steps as data (`authWizard`), the webview posts the
answers (`authWizardSubmit`), and the host checks them as before, reporting a
rejected answer as `authWizardError` (the wizard stays open and nothing is
written) and ending every submission with `authWizardDone`. A connection
failure (`authError`) also leaves the wizard open with its message, so the
answers can be corrected. An open wizard is replayed when the webview
reloads.

The wizard offers OpenRouter, Requesty, OpenAI API Key, Grok (xAI) API Key
and Custom Provider, in that order. OpenAI API Key is a new core preset
(id `openai`, listed after Requesty): OPENAI_API_KEY for OpenAI's Responses
API at https://api.openai.com, with gpt-6.1-sol as the editable default
model. Its installs own only models named
"[OpenAI] …", so models configured by hand with OPENAI_API_KEY stay.

The welcome page title uses the Web Shell welcome screen's size (32px) and
product-name gradient.

